1️⃣ Fare vs Survival

Instead of just looking at passenger class, analyze ticket fare directly.

What to Examine

Average fare of survivors vs non-survivors

Fare distribution

Whether higher-paying passengers survived more

Why This Is Interesting

Passenger class is categorical, but fare is continuous, which gives a more detailed picture.

Possible Insight

Passengers paying higher fares often had:

better cabins

easier access to lifeboats

higher social priority

2️⃣ Age Distribution of Survivors

You already compared adult vs child, but you can go deeper.

What to Examine

Compare survival across multiple age groups:

Children

Teenagers

Young adults

Middle-aged adults

Elderly passengers

Why This Is Interesting

This reveals whether survival preference applied to:

only children

or younger people in general.

Possible Insight

You might find that very young passengers had the highest survival rates.

3️⃣ Passenger Titles (Hidden Social Information)

This is a very interesting one.

The Name column contains titles like:

Mr

Mrs

Miss

Master

Dr

Rev

etc.

What to Examine

Extract titles and analyze survival by title.

Why This Is Powerful

Titles indirectly reveal:

gender

age

social status

Examples:

Master → young boy

Mrs → married woman

Mr → adult male

Possible Insight

You might discover patterns such as:

Masters (boys) surviving more than adult males.

